  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As in the resonance structure of hydrogen azide, it can be seen that number of $\\mathrm{N}-\\mathrm{N}$ bonds is $\\leq 2$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ulI3xDDfrs-jMCBQqsNyj588Er65_mZiXDAWqNbYwug.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nHence for bond (I), bond order will be $ < 2$ whereas for bond (II), number of bond $\\geq 2$. \nThus its bond order will be $>2$.",
    "image": null
  },
